    {
      "topic": "Strict tiny-tail arithmetic",
      "implementation": "Decimal and JavaScript oracle checks now use minimal-subnormal absolute tolerance; a zero in place of a tiny normal coefficient no longer passes. Diagonal NumPy head comparison also requires relative agreement."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Printed coefficient cells",
